// QtRO view contract for the signer UI.
//
// This is the ONE .rep in the wallet stack permitted to carry a password
// parameter. The QML half and this backend are one trust unit — they share a
// plugin identity and one token — so the password crossing between them is not
// a boundary crossing. Every OTHER ui .rep must be free of password parameters,
// and CI asserts that.
//
// `renderLines` is whatever the keystore returned, verbatim. The backend may not
// reformat, elide, truncate or re-order it. That is the authoritative text.
//
// `interpretationLines` is the ONE exception, and it is constrained rather than
// free-form. The backend decodes calldata locally (logos-tx-decoder, linked in,
// offline) so this surface can say "this is a WETH transfer" and not only
// "0xa9059cbb…". Three rules make that safe, and the tests assert them:
//
//   1. DERIVED, NOT FETCHED. The input is `renderLines` itself — the legs are
//      read back out of the text on screen. Nothing is asked of another module
//      or the network, so the interpretation cannot describe bytes other than
//      the ones displayed.
//   2. ADDITIVE, NEVER SUBSTITUTIVE. `renderLines` is shown in full whether or
//      not anything decoded. An empty `interpretationLines` is the normal case
//      for a message, a digest, or an unknown selector.
//   3. SELF-LABELLING. Every line names its own confidence. Only a call to an
//      address the decoder can identify says VERIFIED; a bare 4-byte match says
//      UNVERIFIED, because a selector proves nothing about a contract.
//
// What remains deliberately absent: any field the backend authors from a source
// other than `renderLines`. This plugin still has no client for any wallet,
// chain, RPC or token-list module.
class SignerUi
{
    PROP(QString statusText="Starting" READONLY)
    PROP(QString lastError="" READONLY)

    // The queue, as summaries only — never leg detail.
    PROP(QString pendingJson="[]" READONLY)

    // The request currently on screen. Empty when nothing is being shown.
    PROP(QString renderedHandle="" READONLY)
    PROP(QString renderedBundleId="" READONLY)
    PROP(QString renderedRequester="" READONLY)
    PROP(QStringList renderLines READONLY)

    // Locally decoded reading of the calldata in `renderLines`. Empty whenever
    // nothing decoded, which is not an error. Never a substitute for the above.
    PROP(QStringList interpretationLines READONLY)

    // False until the sheet has been fully visible for the dwell period. Held
    // in C++ so a QML-side edit cannot shorten it.
    PROP(bool dwellElapsed=false READONLY)

    // Re-read the queue from the keystore.
    SLOT(void refresh())
    // Claim a request for display. Demotes whatever was rendered before. False for a
    // handle the keystore does not hold, or one already settled — which a caller pointed
    // here by an intent has to be able to tell apart from a request it can service.
    SLOT(bool acknowledge(QString handle))
    // The human said yes. `bundleId` must be the value that was displayed.
    SLOT(bool approve(QString handle, QString bundleId, QString password))
    // The human said no.
    SLOT(bool reject(QString handle))
    // Close the sheet without deciding (the request stays queued).
    SLOT(void dismiss())

    // A request reached a terminal state: `approved` or `rejected`. Relayed verbatim from
    // the keystore's own event, so it fires however the request settled — from this sheet,
    // from the queue by hand, or from a surface that is not this one at all.
    SIGNAL(settled(QString handle, QString state))
}
